  "text": {
    "intro": "The Dunnage Kite Festival charges by the kite, which has produced some creative definitions of 'one kite'.\nSix fliers are involved. Determine each flier's entry fee, kite, mishap and line.\n- **Flier**: Blaise, Morwenna, Ifeoma, Aurelio, Kipling and Gunnar.\n- **Entry fee** (listed from cheaper to dearer): $2, $4, $6, $8, $10 and $12.\n- **Kite**: a paper sled kite, a box kite, a hand-painted dragon, a delta wing, a seven-metre centipede and a rokkaku fighter.\n- **Mishap**: a lost tail, a snapped spar, a tangled line, a sudden lull, a trespassing dog and a tree.\n- **Line**: fishing monofilament, parcel string, hemp cord, waxed cotton, nylon twine and kevlar thread.\nEvery flier has a different entry fee, kite, mishap and line, so within each category every item is used exactly once.",
